Z||000001||88 Database Nut||05-17-2000||03:55 PM||||Welcome Back Count!  So, you've gone from a 5 letter F word to a 4 letter one, not that big of a deal!<P>Say, sorry to be so morbid, but could you send me some info on that car your sister wrecked (she was ok, right?)?  As you might know, I am working on documenting as many of the '88s as possible, if your's is toast I'd sure like to record that fact.  All I need is the VIN and a brief color and transmission description. I don't need any personal info, but that's welcome if you want, along with special info on options or really anything else you might want to say about your car.  So far, we've got info on 1082 cars, let me know and I'll shoot you a copy of the summary.<P>Good Luck if you choose to buy another, there are alot for sale online, if you need a pointer just holler.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||05-17-2000||07:24 PM||||Sorry to hear about that GT.  Its terrible to loose your car in an accident.  I assume you meant to say a 93 Probe (they made them 89-97).  Is it a base, or a GT?  The 4 cyl Probe are nice cars... not very fast but neither were the 4 cyl Fieros.  I own a 97 Probe SE as my daily driver along with my Fiero Formula.  I can give you a couple boards to check out for the Probe.  But remember, there are a lot more punk kids riding around in Probes than there are in Fieros.  They are a little less forgiving and tolerant of other ideas... they love to flame "ricers" even though Probes have Mazda drivetrains... and could technically be called rice burners too.  Anyway, check out the sites.  They are good at helping with repair problems... almost as good as our Fiero people here!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.probetalk.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.probetalk.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.webcentrix.net/probe/messageboard/index.lasso" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webcentrix.net/probe/messageboard/index.lasso</A> <P>I am John 97 PSE on webcentrix and Fformula88 on the probetalk!  Also feel free to email me with any Probe ?'s you may have.  Also, GET ANOTHER FIERO.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||frontal lobe||05-17-2000||11:06 PM||||I had the 2.2liter turbo-charged intercooled engine that used to be in the probe GT, but in the grown-ups version, the Mazda 626 4-door sedan.  Yeah, it looked like a grampa-car on the outside, but that thing really hauled!  Yes, it had some turbo-lag, and under power it torque-steered like crazy, but it was a sleeper<P>So, if you have the probe GT, you are in business until you can afford another Fiero.||||reg||1
